  PRIMARY  the CALIBRATED cell from sensefit: sigma 56.0 Hz at tau 60 ms,
           at the shipped 905 ms round trip
           open  107.9   best   51.9 at gain 0.00100   removed  51.9%   CLEARS THE 25% BAR
           measured trial accuracy here 0.753  (selfcode 0.623, sensefit's own decoder 0.764)
           same sigma at the other correlation times:  0 ms 55.9%   60 ms 51.9%  
           bracket on sigma: 0 Hz -> 55.9%,  92 Hz -> 47.9%  BOTH clear the bar

  GUARD  correlation axis live AT THE OPERATING POINT?  white removes 55.9%
         and the measured tau 51.9%, 4.0 points apart -> INERT HERE. Read the top of the
         sigma ladder for where it bites: correlation costs nothing at the
         measured noise and a great deal at 2-4x it, so the operating point
         sits below the level where the error's TIME STRUCTURE matters.

  THE CREATURE'S OWN ERROR SIGNAL IS ENOUGH. At the sensor sensefit
  measured -- 56 Hz input-referred at tau 60 ms, against an F1
  whose own sd is 21 Hz -- feedback still removes 51.9% of the
  open-loop error through the SHIPPED 905 ms round trip. That is more
  than the entire measured naming effect, so the learning rule is worth
  building and its target is a controller at gain 0.00100 with the
  attenuation undone.
